# Live runtime state, not real config (2026-08-11, real bug fix) - per
# the owner: "when we redo or make changes to the reports tray it autopopulates
# with reports we've already seen." These get rewritten continuously by
# the running system (mark_report_viewed.py, the scheduler, etc.), never
# meaningfully "committed" - every prior commit of them was just whatever
# seed value happened to be in the working tree at commit time. Tracking
# them meant every branch checkout/merge silently overwrote the real,
# live value with a stale committed one - traced live to reports_viewed.json
# specifically resetting to its empty {} seed mid-merge, making every
# already-read report look unread again. Untracking (not deleting) so the
# working tree's real, current value is never again at the mercy of git
# operations. project_catalog.json/usage_resets.json aren't listed here -
# those are genuinely-versioned config, unmodified all session.
config/daily_goal.json
config/last_break.json
config/reports_viewed.json
config/scheduled_tasks_snapshot.json
config/session_reset.json
